      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Given that $a$ is three times $b$, we can write this as $a=3b$. Similarly, since $b$ is twice $c$, we have $b=2c$. And since $c$ is four times $d$, we get $c=4d$. Now we can substitute these relationships into the expression $\\frac{a\\cdot c}{b\\cdot d}$.\n\nSubstituting $a=3b$, $b=2c$, and $c=4d$ into the expression, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{a\\cdot c}{b\\cdot d} = \\frac{3b\\cdot c}{b\\cdot d} = \\frac{3b\\cdot 4d}{b\\cdot d}\n\\]\n\nSimplifying this expression, we find:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3\\cdot 4}{1} = 3\\cdot 4 = \\boxed{12}\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of $\\frac{a\\cdot c}{b\\cdot d}$ is 12.",
