    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Let's start by expressing the given relationships in terms of equations. We are given that:\n\n1. \\( a = 3b \\)\n2. \\( b = 2c \\)\n3. \\( c = 4d \\)\n\nWe need to find the value of \\(\\frac{a \\cdot c}{b \\cdot d}\\). Let's substitute the expressions for \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\) in terms of \\(d\\) into the expression.\n\nFirst, express \\(a\\) in terms of \\(d\\):\n\n\\[\na = 3b\n\\]\n\nNext, express \\(b\\) in terms of \\(d\\):\n\n\\[\nb = 2c\n\\]\n\nFinally, express \\(c\\) in terms of \\(d\\):\n\n\\[\nc = 4d\n\\]\n\nNow substitute these expressions back into the original equation:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{a \\cdot c}{b \\cdot d}\n\\]\n\nStarting with \\(a\\):\n\n\\[\na = 3b \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad a = 3(2c) \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad a = 6c\n\\]\n\nThen, using \\(c = 4d\\):\n\n\\[\na = 6c \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad a = 6(4d) \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad a = 24d\n\\]\n\nNow substitute \\(a = 24d\\), \\(b = 2c = 2(4d) = 8d\\), and \\(c = 4d\\) into the original expression:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{a \\cdot c}{b \\cdot d} = \\frac{(24d) \\cdot (4d)}{(8d) \\cdot d}\n\\]\n\nSimplify the numerator and the denominator:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{(24d) \\cdot (4d)}{(8d) \\cdot d} = \\frac{96d^2}{8d^2}\n\\]\n\nThe \\(d^2\\) terms cancel out:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{96d^2}{8d^2} = \\frac{96}{8} = 12\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(\\frac{a \\cdot c}{b \\cdot d}\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{12}\n\\]",
